A||||4||Philphine||easiest way to end up with power windows?||||1||
Z||000000||Philphine||11-08-2001||10:35 AM||||<BR>got some subs i've been waiting for but i need to switch to power windows before i can start working on putting them in. since i need a paint job anyway would it be easiest to find and swap doors? find the mechanisms and put them in mine (my doors are in good shape and hinges and alignment are good) or get some of the aftermarket type? i'm thinking aftermarket 'cause it seems simplest, but i'm open to suggestions. thanks for any help.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||11-08-2001||10:40 AM||||the doors are cheap, Id get used ones with them already in. Youll even end up with spare parts if you ever need them like windows, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadaver||11-10-2001||09:35 PM||||The easiest way I found was to get the factory wiring/switches/regulators from a power and swap out the parts in my doors. doing it that way there is no paint work involved like if you swap door skins and no alignment headaches to deal with like swaping doors. I would never use a "universal" kit. Why try to deal with something that might fit when you know thw factory stuff will fit great. I have also added power locks and mirrors, hot back glass and everyother option to many cars using factory parts.||||reg||1
Z||000003||U Wanna Race||11-12-2001||12:28 PM||||If you dont want to put much work into this project, you may want to look at some universal electric window kits.  Colibri makes a set that dont seem to be bad, I beleive they run in the range of $150.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||11-12-2001||12:51 PM||||some aftermarket kits are pretty simple but less reliable. I had some on a Dodge van that were just little boxes that you mounted right over the roll up crank shaft, then just ran a hot and ground wire. They worked ok, just had this ugly 3X6 inch plastic box on your door panel. Some of the better kits go inside the door. Changing the doors is no big deal, keep your old good hinges. No painting either, just swap the door skins.||||reg||1
